The memory bandwidth benchmark on the machine's GPU, on small arrays: each
kernel is an SPMD kernel, and the arrays' final values are right.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -O2 -fopenmp -fdo-loops --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/../../benchmarks/bandwidth/bandwidth.m -o %t
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY LIBOMPTARGET_INFO=16 BANDWIDTH_ARRAY_SIZE=100003 BANDWIDTH_NUM_TIMES=5 %t 2> %t.info | FileCheck %s
RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=INFO < %t.info
CHECK: Running kernels 5 times
CHECK-NOT: Validation failed
CHECK: Function    MBytes/sec  Min (sec)   Max         Average
CHECK-NEXT: Copy
CHECK-NEXT: Mul
CHECK-NEXT: Add
CHECK-NEXT: Triad
CHECK-NEXT: Dot
INFO: Launching kernel {{.*}}bandwidth.init_{{.*}} in SPMD mode
INFO: Launching kernel {{.*}}bandwidth.copy_{{.*}} in SPMD mode
INFO: Launching kernel {{.*}}bandwidth.dot_{{.*}} in SPMD mode
INFO-NOT: Generic

The arrays stay on the device for the runs: after the region's copies to it, no
kernel copies any of them, until the region copies them back.
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY LIBOMPTARGET_INFO=32 BANDWIDTH_ARRAY_SIZE=100003 BANDWIDTH_NUM_TIMES=5 %t 2> %t.copies > /dev/null
RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=COPIES < %t.copies
COPIES: Copying data from host to device, {{.*}}Name=A, at {{.*}}bandwidth.m:[[REGION:[0-9]+]]:
COPIES: Copying data from host to device, {{.*}}Name=B, at {{.*}}bandwidth.m:[[REGION]]:
COPIES: Copying data from host to device, {{.*}}Name=C, at {{.*}}bandwidth.m:[[REGION]]:
COPIES-NOT: Size=800032
COPIES: Copying data from device to host, {{.*}}Size=800032, {{.*}}bandwidth.m:[[REGION]]:
